[section:std_tuple C++ Tuple]

C++ tuples with arithmetic elements can be used as points within Boost.Geometry.

[heading Description]

A `std::tuple`, such as `std::tuple<double, double>`, is optionally adapted to
the Boost.Geometry point concept. Its elements may have different types;
Boost.Geometry reports the first type as its
[link geometry.reference.core.coordinate_type coordinate_type].

A tuple can be the point type used by the linestring, polygon, segment, box,
and ring models.

[heading Model of]
[link geometry.reference.concepts.concept_point Point Concept]

[heading Header]
`#include <boost/geometry/geometries/adapted/std_tuple.hpp>`

__not_in_boost_geometry_hpp__

